---
layout: base.njk
title: Contact | The Web3 Family
description: Call, text, email, or schedule a call with Christopher Clarke directly.
---
<!-- CONTACT -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Let's talk.</h1>
    <p class="subhead">Pick whatever is easiest. Every message comes straight to me.</p>

    <div class="contact-grid">
      <div class="contact-ways">
        <a class="way way-primary" href="https://calendly.com/aweb3dad/15-minute-greeting" onclick="Calendly.initPopupWidget({url:'https://calendly.com/aweb3dad/15-minute-greeting'});return false;">
          <span class="way-label">Schedule a call with me</span>
          <span class="way-detail">A free 15 minute call on my calendar</span>
          <span class="way-go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
        <a class="way" href="tel:+13107036003">
          <span class="way-label">Call or text</span>
          <span class="way-detail">(310) 703-6003</span>
          <span class="way-go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
        <a class="way" href="mailto:christopher@theweb3family.com">
          <span class="way-label">Email</span>
          <span class="way-detail">christopher@theweb3family.com</span>
          <span class="way-go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
        <p class="contact-place">Based in Inglewood, California. Working with nonprofits everywhere.</p>
      </div>

      {#
        This is a stand-in for real Splitform embed, per direct request
        ("This needs to be a form"). Not the real Splitform widget: that
        still needs the actual embed snippet or hosted form URL from
        Christopher's own Splitform account, which nobody but him can
        pull, and loading it will be a deliberate, confirmed exception
        to the site's zero-client-JS rule (section 9), the same kind of
        tradeoff Microsoft Clarity already is. In the meantime this is a
        plain mailto: form: it needs no backend and adds no JavaScript,
        but it only works if the visitor's device has an email app
        configured to handle mailto: links, which not everyone does
        (many people read mail only in a browser tab). Swap this whole
        block for the real Splitform embed once that's in hand.
      #}
      <form class="contact-form contact-card" action="mailto:christopher@theweb3family.com" method="post" enctype="text/plain">
        <h2 class="contact-card-title">Send a note</h2>
        <label>Name
          <input type="text" name="Name" autocomplete="name" required>
        </label>
        <label>Email
          <input type="email" name="Email" autocomplete="email" required>
        </label>
        <label><span>Organization <span class="optional">(optional)</span></span>
          <input type="text" name="Organization" autocomplete="organization">
        </label>
        <label>How can I help?
          <textarea name="Message" rows="5" required></textarea>
        </label>
        <button type="submit" class="cta"><span>Send</span></button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
